    "advice_r1_title": "Recovery is when you grow",
    "advice_r1_body": "Training is the stimulus, recovery is the adaptation. Schedule at least one full rest day per week, and treat it as part of the program — not a missed workout.",
    "advice_r2_title": "Listen to your body",
    "advice_r2_body": "Persistent soreness, low energy, or poor mood across several days is feedback. Pull back the intensity for a few sessions before pushing again.",
    "advice_r3_title": "Move on rest days",
    "advice_r3_body": "Light walking, easy mobility, or gentle stretching helps recovery more than complete inactivity. Keep blood flowing without adding training stress.",
    "advice_n1_title": "Protein supports adaptation",
    "advice_n1_body": "Aim for a protein source at every meal. Roughly 1.6–2.0 g per kg of body weight per day supports recovery and muscle building during structured training.",
    "advice_n2_title": "Eat enough to train",
    "advice_n2_body": "Under-fueling causes low energy, poor sleep, and stalled progress. If performance and recovery are slipping, food intake is often the first thing to check.",
    "advice_n3_title": "Hydrate consistently",
    "advice_n3_body": "Dehydration drops performance before you feel thirsty. Sip water throughout the day, not just around workouts. Pale yellow urine is a good rough check.",
    "advice_s1_title": "Sleep is the strongest recovery tool",
    "advice_s1_body": "Most adults need 7–9 hours. Hormones that drive recovery, mood, and appetite all depend on it. Protect bedtime like you would a training session.",
    "advice_s2_title": "Build a wind-down routine",
    "advice_s2_body": "Dim lights an hour before bed, put screens away, keep the room cool. A consistent routine signals the body it's time to switch off and improves sleep quality over time.",
    "advice_s3_title": "Same time every day",
    "advice_s3_body": "A regular sleep and wake time — even on weekends — stabilises your body clock and makes both falling asleep and waking up easier.",
    "advice_m1_title": "Show up on the hard days",
